{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Glossary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Glossary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":110,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.verschiebung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.verschiebung","kind":"def","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L344-L344","doc":"Verschiebung endomorphism `V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.frobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.frobenius","kind":"def","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L342-L342","doc":"Frobenius endomorphism `F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.carrier","kind":"def","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L340-L340","doc":"The carrier module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L338-L338","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FIsocrystal","kind":"structure","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L332-L344","doc":"**F-Isocrystal**: A module over the Dieudonné ring\n`ℚ_p⟨F, V⟩ / (FV − p)`, where the Frobenius endomorphism plays the\nrole of Levi-form contraction.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:f-isocrystal}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature.section_","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature.section_","kind":"def","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L328-L328","doc":"The self-dual curvature as a section `M → ℝ` (simplified). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature.manifold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature.manifold","kind":"def","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L326-L326","doc":"The manifold carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature.mk","kind":"ctor","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L324-L324","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.SelfDualCurvature","kind":"structure","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L320-L328","doc":"**Self-Dual Curvature**: The projection `F_A⁺ ∈ Γ(Λ⁺ H* ⊗ Ad(P))`\nof the curvature onto the self-dual subbundle of `Λ² H*`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:self-dual-curvature}` (defined within). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject.adjointAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject.adjointAction","kind":"def","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L318-L318","doc":"The adjoint action map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject.carrier","kind":"def","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L316-L316","doc":"The carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject.mk","kind":"ctor","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L314-L314","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.AdjointObject","kind":"structure","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L309-L318","doc":"**Adjoint Object** `Ad(A)`: the object `A` with the conjugation coaction\n`a ↦ Σ a₍₁₎ b S(a₍₂₎)`.  In the ℂ realisation this is the adjoint\nbundle `Ad(P)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-observable-universe}`, item (ii). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.proj","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L307-L307","doc":"Bundle projection `π : P → M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.total","kind":"def","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L305-L305","doc":"The total space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.group","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.group","kind":"def","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L303-L303","doc":"The structure group carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.base","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L301-L301","doc":"The base manifold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle.mk","kind":"ctor","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L299-L299","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.PrincipalBundle","kind":"structure","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L294-L307","doc":"**Principal Bundle**: A principal `G`-bundle `P → M` whose holonomy\nreduces to `SO(3) ⊂ SU(2)/{±I}`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:c-quantum-universe}`, item (iv).\nMathlib: `Mathlib.Topology.FiberBundle.Basic` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.proj","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L292-L292","doc":"Bundle projection `π : E → M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.total","kind":"def","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L290-L290","doc":"The total space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.base","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L288-L288","doc":"The base manifold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.StateBundle.mk","kind":"ctor","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L286-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.StateBundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.StateBundle","kind":"structure","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L282-L292","doc":"**State Bundle**: The associated bundle `E = P ×_G ℂP¹ → M` where\n`SU(2)` acts on `ℂP¹` by Möbius transformations.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:c-quantum-universe}`, item (v). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.star_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.star_sq","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L280-L280","doc":"Involutivity: `*_H² = id` (when `dim_ℝ H = 4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.star","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L278-L278","doc":"The Hodge star operator `*_H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.forms","kind":"def","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L276-L276","doc":"The type of 2-forms on `H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH.mk","kind":"ctor","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L274-L274","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.HodgeStarH","kind":"structure","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L268-L280","doc":"**Hodge Star** on the horizontal distribution `H`: the operator\n`*_H : Λ² H* → Λ² H*` determined by the Webster metric, satisfying\n`*_H² = id` when `dim_ℝ H = 4`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:instanton}` (referenced within).\nMathlib: `Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian.op","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian.op","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L266-L266","doc":"The Laplacian operator `Δ_q : forms → forms`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian.forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian.forms","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L264-L264","doc":"The type of forms on which the Laplacian acts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian.mk","kind":"ctor","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L262-L262","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QLaplacian","kind":"structure","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L258-L266","doc":"**q-Laplacian**: The operator `Δ_q = d_q δ_q + δ_q d_q` whose kernel\ndefines q-harmonic forms (particles).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-harmonic-form}` (referenced within). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.energy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.energy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L256-L256","doc":"The energy is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.energy","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L254-L254","doc":"The functional evaluated on a connection (abstract). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.manifold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.manifold","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L252-L252","doc":"The manifold carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional.mk","kind":"ctor","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L250-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.YangMillsFunctional","kind":"structure","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L245-L256","doc":"**Yang–Mills Functional**: The gauge-theoretic energy functional\n`∫_M ‖F_A|_H‖² θ ∧ (dθ)ⁿ` whose critical points are Yang–Mills\nconnections.  Instantons are absolute minimisers.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:instanton}` (referenced within). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.genK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.genK","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L243-L243","doc":"Generator `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.genF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.genF","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L241-L241","doc":"Generator `F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.genE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.genE","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L239-L239","doc":"Generator `E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.q","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L237-L237","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.carrier","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L235-L235","doc":"Carrier type of the integral form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L233-L233","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LusztigIntegralForm","kind":"structure","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L226-L243","doc":"**Lusztig Integral Form**: The `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`-subalgebra\n`U^ℤ_q(𝔰𝔲(2))` of `U_q(𝔰𝔲(2))` generated by `K^{±1}` and the\ndivided powers `E^{(n)} = Eⁿ/[n]_q!`, `F^{(n)} = Fⁿ/[n]_q!`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:substrate-parameter}` (referenced within).\nRef: [lusztig1993] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField.field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField.field","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L224-L224","doc":"The Reeb field as a map `M → TM` (simplified to `M → M`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField.manifold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField.manifold","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L222-L222","doc":"The manifold carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L220-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.ReebVectorField","kind":"structure","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L215-L224","doc":"**Reeb Vector Field**: The unique vector field `ξ` on a contact manifold\n`(M, θ)` characterised by `ι_ξ dθ = 0` and `θ(ξ) = 1`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:reeb-decomposition}` (defined within)\nMathlib: No direct equivalent; builds on vector field infrastructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.s","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L213-L213","doc":"Signature parameter `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.r","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L211-L211","doc":"Signature parameter `r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.metric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.metric","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L209-L209","doc":"The metric tensor `g_θ : H × H → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.horizontal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.horizontal","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L207-L207","doc":"The horizontal distribution `H` as a type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric.mk","kind":"ctor","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.WebsterMetric","kind":"structure","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L199-L213","doc":"**Webster Metric**: The pseudo-Riemannian metric `g_θ` of signature\n`(2r, 2s)` on the horizontal distribution `H`, induced by the contact\nform `θ` and the Levi form `L_θ`.\n\nLaTeX: used in `\\label{def:c-quantum-universe}`, item (ii).\nMathlib: `Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LeviForm.pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LeviForm.pairing","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L197-L197","doc":"The Hermitian pairing `L_θ : H × H → ℝ` (real part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LeviForm.horizontal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LeviForm.horizontal","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L195-L195","doc":"The horizontal distribution `H` as a type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LeviForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LeviForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L193-L193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.LeviForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.LeviForm","kind":"structure","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L186-L197","doc":"**Levi Form**: The Hermitian form `L_θ : H × H → ℂ` on the horizontal\ndistribution `H = ker θ`, defined by `L_θ(V, W) = −i dθ(V, W̄)`.\nNon-degeneracy of the Levi form is the defining property of a CR manifold\nof hypersurface type.\n\nLaTeX: used in `\\label{def:c-quantum-universe}`, item (i).\nMathlib: `Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic` (sesquilinear forms) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup.order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup.order","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L182-L182","doc":"The group order is 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup.carrier","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L180-L180","doc":"Carrier type for group elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L178-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BinaryDihedralGroup","kind":"structure","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L173-L182","doc":"**Binary Dihedral Group**: `Dic₃ ⊂ SU(2)` of order 12, lifting S₃\nvia the double cover `SU(2) → SO(3)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:binary-dihedral}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.mul","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L171-L171","doc":"Composition of braids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.one","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L169-L169","doc":"The identity braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.carrier","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L167-L167","doc":"Carrier type for braid group elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BraidGroup","kind":"structure","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L160-L171","doc":"**Braid Group B₃**: The braid group on 3 strands, presented as\n`⟨σ₁, σ₂ | σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂⟩`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:braid-group}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.derivation","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L156-L156","doc":"The universal derivation `d : A → Ω¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.differentials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.differentials","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L154-L154","doc":"The module of differentials `Ω¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.algebra","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The algebra `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials.mk","kind":"ctor","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.KahlerDifferentials","kind":"structure","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L145-L156","doc":"**Kähler Differentials**: `Ω¹(A) = ker(m : A ⊗ A → A)`, the universal\nfirst-order differential calculus.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:kahler-differentials}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.proj","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L143-L143","doc":"Jet projection to the base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.fibre","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L141-L141","doc":"The fibre type (first-order differentials). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.base","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L139-L139","doc":"The base type (algebra `A`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.JetProlongation","kind":"structure","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**Jet Prolongation**: The first jet bundle `J¹E` represented\ncategorically by `A ⊗ Ω¹(A)` where `Ω¹(A) = ker(m : A ⊗ A → A)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:jet-prolongation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.substrateParameter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.substrateParameter","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L123-L128","doc":"**Substrate Parameter**: `q(p) = 1 + |⟨L_θ, F_A⁺⟩|(p)` — couples\nchiral curvature to contact geometry on Bring's surface.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:substrate-parameter}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L121-L121","doc":"Euler characteristic is −6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.genus","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Genus of Bring's surface is 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.carrier","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface.mk","kind":"ctor","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.BringsSurface","kind":"structure","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L109-L121","doc":"**Bring's Surface**: The maximally symmetric CR manifold of genus 4,\nwith Euler characteristic χ = −6, defined by Σ x_j^k = 0 for k = 1,2,3\nin CP⁴.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:brings-surface}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.n_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.n_pos","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L107-L107","doc":"Non-degeneracy: `n ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.n","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L105-L105","doc":"CR dimension `n ≥ 1` (real dimension is `2n + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.toTopSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.toTopSpace","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.carrier","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The underlying topological space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.CRManifold.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.CRManifold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.CRManifold","kind":"structure","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L94-L107","doc":"**CR Manifold Structure**: A pseudo-Hermitian structure with Levi\ndistribution, Reeb vector field, and Webster metric.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:cr-manifold}`\nMathlib: `Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L90-L90","doc":"q is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.q","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The deformation parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.carrier","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The carrier type of the quantum group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.QuantumGaugeGroup","kind":"structure","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L79-L90","doc":"**Quantum Gauge Group**: The quantum group `G_q = Aut⊗(ω)` reconstructed\nvia Tannaka-Krein duality from the fibre functor.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-gauge-group}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.mapObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.mapObj","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The functor map on objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.target","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Target category (vector spaces). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.source","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Source category (representation category). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FibreFunctor","kind":"structure","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L65-L77","doc":"**Fibre Functor**: An exact faithful k-linear monoidal functor\n`ω : C → Vect_k` used in Tannaka-Krein reconstruction.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:fibre-functor}`\nMathlib: `Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.quantumParameter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.quantumParameter","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L57-L63","doc":"**Quantum Deformation Parameter**: The parameter `q ∈ k×` governing\nthe Hopf algebra structure.  At `q = 1` we recover the classical\ncocommutative case.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-parameter}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → ℝ` (non-degenerate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.antipode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.antipode","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Antipode `S : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.counit","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Counit `ε : A → unit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.comul","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Comultiplication `Δ : A → A × A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.unit","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Unit element `η : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.mul","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Multiplication `μ : A ⊗ A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.carrier","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The carrier type of the underlying object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Glossary.FrobeniusHopfObject","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Glossary.lean#L33-L55","doc":"**Frobenius-Hopf Object**: An object `A` in a rigid monoidal category\nequipped with a Hopf algebra structure `(μ, η, Δ, ε, S)` and a\nFrobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙` satisfying non-degeneracy.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:frobenius-hopf}`\nMathlib: No direct equivalent — builds on `Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category`\nUniverses: objects in `u`, morphisms in `v` ","signatureChunk":0}]}